  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.4. Increased capacity of Member States to provide adequate labour protection to workers in diverse forms of work arrangements, including on digital labour platforms, and in informal employment</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">By the end of 2023, the Albanian State Labour Inspectorate and Social Services (ASLISS) has improved its capabilities to detect undeclared and underdeclared work. The ASLISS has a new Risk Assessment System which, using Data Mining and Machine Learning, can detect undeclared work with a 30% increase of accuracy than the previous one. Furthermore, the new Risk Assessment System has been merged with the upgraded Electronic Case Management System (the Matrix of Penalties) into one software to improve inspection planning and data processing and analytics efficiency. The social partners have welcomed these improvements in the functioning of the ASLISS. The ILO provided technical assistance to develop the Risk Assessment System and to optimise the Albanian State Labour Inspectorate and Social Services (ASLISS) processes regarding inspection planning, and data processing. The ILO conducted a study that indicated that the Data Mining and Machine Learning Risk Assessment System assessed the accuracy of the new tool and shared the results with the ASLISS. The ILO upgraded the Matrix of Penalties and merged it with the Risk Assessment System. The ILO also trained all inspectors in using the Matrix of Penalties and all relevant supervisors in using the Matrix of Penalties and the Risk Assessment System.</narrative>
   </description>
