  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Decision of the Council of Ministers no. 265, dated 27.04.2023 &#x201C;On some changes to the Decision no. 1039, dated 4.12.2013, of the Council of Ministers, &#x201C;On the functioning of the tripartite National Labour Council and designation of the representatives of the Council of Ministers within this Council&#x201D; provides an improved functioning of the tripartite National Labour Council (NLC).
The recent amendment enables the establishment of permanent specialized committees of the NLC. The members to the committees have been appointed. The ILO promoted and facilitated tripartite and bipartite consultations and dialogue at national, regional and enterprise level in relation to labour dispute prevention and resolution and supported the conduct of the nation-wide awareness campaign on Amicable Labour Dispute Settlement through multiple communication channels and tools.</narrative>
   </description>
